  "prefLabel": "Ed 1019.09 Vending Routes",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 1019.09 Vending Routes.\n\n(a) Individual vending routes shall be established by the program when deemed appropriate by SBVI, and only when accepted by the state committee of licensed managers by a simple majority vote.\n\n(b) Once a vending route is established it shall remain an intact route. When the manager no longer wishes to, or cannot, serve one or more of the locations on the established vending route, the vending route as a whole shall go out to bid as a single vending location.\n\n(c) Altering the composition of a vending route requires the submission of a written proposal which shall be jointly approved by the program and the state committee of licensed managers.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1, #2, and #3 at chapter heading for Ed 1000) #13231, eff 7-13-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1000.html"
